From 1ca677a3c081341e5633178f077b4b67df320dfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <services.claude@accounts.ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 09:38:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: patch 0213 -- silence throttle: never sleep inside the
 application's pump

Why: PlayDevice's silence-skip path sleeps 10 ms (SDL/0050's quiescence
throttle, moved from GetDeviceBuf into PlayDevice by 0054) to stop the
background playback thread spinning through Iterate while nothing plays.
PlayDevice is also reached from the application's own loop through
SDL_DOSAudioPump() (SDL/0067). A port that pumps from its game loop (dosags:
AGS_DISABLE_THREADS, a poll per tick and about one per ms inside its frame
wait) therefore slept its GAME LOOP 10 ms on every silent buffer: on a 486,
pump mean 11.0 ms per poll and 27.3 stable ticks/s sound-on against 37.5
sound-off (dosags LAB-S32.md 16).

What: SDL_DOSAudioPump() brackets its Iterate call with a counter, and the
SDL_Delay(10) runs only when that counter is zero. Every other path -- the
device thread included -- keeps the throttle exactly as before, so a port
without an application pump (doskutsu's steady state) sees no change. The
skip itself is unchanged on every path: the silent buffer is still not
written, so the Sound Blaster still drains to its idle pause. Structural,
not a hint.

Why not thread identity (the first version): device->thread is assigned
only after SDL_CreateThread returns, and on the cooperative scheduler the
new audio thread runs first. It would see no device thread, skip the sleep,
and -- with SDL/0086's yield killswitched and silence at open -- loop
WaitDevice/PlayDevice without sleeping or yielding, so main would never run
again. Before this patch the SDL_Delay(10) yielded there; with the counter
it still does. (Found in review by the dosags main worker.)

An OpenDevice banner line names the rule.
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 37 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 32e947b68..272b6098a 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -822,6 +822,12 @@ volatile bool g_dos_audio_force_dsp_pause = false;
    when the hint is exactly "1". */
 static bool g_dos_audio_no_bg_thread = false;
 
+/* DOS-PORT patch 0213: nonzero while SDL_DOSAudioPump() (the application's own
+   loop) is running Iterate. PlayDevice skips its silence throttle only then; see
+   the comment there. A counter, not a bool, so a nested pump cannot clear it
+   early; touched only under device->lock. */
+static int g_dos_in_app_pump = 0;
+
 /* DOS-PORT patch 0144: OpenDevice bisection diagnostic (S7).
    S7-irq7-lpt1-hypothesis-refuted-2026-09-14.md: what's now common to
    every collapsed real-hardware arm (thread present/absent, DMA active/
@@ -3715,6 +3721,10 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
 
     SDL_Log("SoundBlaster opened!");
 
+    /* DOS-PORT patch 0213: say which paths may sleep on a silent buffer. */
+    dos_port_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0213 silence throttle skipped inside SDL_DOSAudioPump() only "
+                     "(device thread %s)", g_dos_audio_no_bg_thread ? "absent" : "present");
+
     /* DOS-PORT patch 0143: banner for SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_NO_BG_THREAD=1
        (the actual behavior -- impl->ProvidesOwnCallbackThread -- is
        resolved earlier, at Init() time, since SDL_audio.c's OpenAudioDevice
@@ -4032,7 +4042,9 @@ bool SDL_DOSAudioPump(void)
        consistency with WaitDevice's own room check (line 720-721 of
        this file) -- same definition of "room" = same predicate
        boundary. */
+    g_dos_in_app_pump++;   /* DOS-PORT patch 0213: PlayDevice must not sleep the app's loop */
     bool iter_ok = SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate(device);
+    g_dos_in_app_pump--;
     bool has_room = false;
 
     if (iter_ok) {
@@ -4573,7 +4585,31 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_PlayDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device, const Uint8 *buf
                ISR increments consecutive-silent-IRQ counter -> DSP
                auto-engage idle-pause fires when threshold met -> IRQ-5
                stops -> fps recovered. Same mechanism as SDL/0050. */
-            SDL_Delay(10);  /* throttle ~100 iter/sec when quiescent;
+            /* DOS-PORT patch 0213: never sleep inside the application's pump.
+               The throttle below exists to stop the background playback
+               thread spinning through Iterate while there is nothing to
+               play. PlayDevice is also reached from the application's own
+               loop through SDL_DOSAudioPump() (SDL/0067), and there the
+               10 ms sleep lands on the game loop instead: a port that pumps
+               once per game tick lost ~10-11 ms of every silent tick (dosags
+               S32S1 on a 486: pump mean 11.0 ms/tick, stable 27.3 vs 37.5
+               sound-off). The pump caller paces its own calls (dosags: one
+               per tick, plus about one per ms inside its own frame wait,
+               which only polls while the wait has room for a poll), so it
+               needs no throttle from here. The skip itself
+               is unchanged on both paths: the silent buffer is still not
+               written, so the SB still drains to its idle pause.
+               Decided structurally -- is this call inside SDL_DOSAudioPump()? --
+               not by a hint and not by thread identity: every other path,
+               the device thread included, keeps the throttle exactly as
+               before. (Thread identity was tried first and has a startup
+               window: device->thread is assigned only after SDL_CreateThread
+               returns, and on the cooperative scheduler the new thread runs
+               first; with SDL/0086's yield killswitched and silence at open
+               it would loop without sleeping or yielding and main would never
+               run again.) */
+            if (g_dos_in_app_pump == 0)
+                SDL_Delay(10);  /* throttle ~100 iter/sec when quiescent;
                                prevents CPU spin under cooperative
                                scheduler. Held under device->lock per
                                PlaybackAudioThreadIterate (SDL_audio.c:
